  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the total number of bonds between chromium and oxygen atoms in chromate and dichromate ions is ______________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Chromate ion <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/edf1035d-37b8-4873-b221-85d45a2e5a3f.jpeg\" /><br /><br />&nbsp;Dichromate ion <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/783c3bf1-3833-4596-9b9e-9f080ba21eb2.jpeg\" /></p><p>The chromate ion (CrO42&ndash;) has a tetrahedral shape, whereas dichromate ion has two tetrahedral units with one common oxygen having Cr-O-Cr bond angle of 126&deg;. Both are oxyanions of chromium in the 6+ oxidation state and are moderately strong oxidizing agents.</p>",
